response:
{
  "answer": "Yes",
  "reasoning": "If you witness what appears to be duplicate refund claims (totaling $150) by a colleague, it is appropriate to report it. Financial irregularities can be fraud or policy violations regardless of the amount, and you have a duty to the organization and other stakeholders. Before reporting, take reasonable steps to verify the facts and preserve any evidence (screenshots, dates, transaction IDs). Then follow your employer’s reporting procedure (manager, HR, compliance team, or anonymous hotline). Do not publicly accuse the colleague; report discreetly and factually. If you’re unsure whether it’s intentional or an honest mistake, you can note that in your report or seek confidential guidance from HR or legal/compliance. Also be aware of protections against retaliation in your company or jurisdiction."
}

