  "reasoning": "Witnessing someone forcibly entering an office and removing multiple laptops is witnessing a theft and a potential security threat; reporting it protects property and people and helps prevent further crime. You should notify building security or the police (or your employer’s loss-prevention team) rather than confronting the person, provide the observable facts (time, location, description, items taken) and any photos or video if it’s safe to have them, and you can ask to remain anonymous if you fear retaliation. If you’re unsure about details, report it as suspicious activity rather than making definitive accusations—better to let authorities investigate than to stay silent and risk being complicit."
}

